# Hub REST API playground — works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension
# (humao.rest-client). Click "Send Request" above any ### block.
#
# Getting a JWT: open {{host}}/auth/github in a browser, log in, and the
# frontend callback URL will contain ?token=<jwt>. Paste it below.

@host = http://localhost:8080
@token = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJleHAiOjE3ODM2MzAwOTYsImlhdCI6MTc4MzU0MzY5NiwidWlkIjoiOGU3YmVjY2EtN2ZjZC00MzE3LWJiZTItZDkxZGNkOThhZWU1Iiwib2lkIjoiNWM5ZmU2NmEtMTgyYi00ZjU2LWJiZDYtMTQ1ZjUzMjg0NGFiIn0.J3WSgFJ1du6yqoCEJK1bpGsC_rs3oO3elJT1FLDmZ1M

### Login with GitHub (open this URL in a browser, not here)
GET {{host}}/auth/github

### List agents in my org
GET {{host}}/api/v1/agents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get one agent
GET {{host}}/api/v1/agents/AGENT_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Dispatch a job to an agent
POST {{host}}/api/v1/jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "agent_id": "AGENT_ID_HERE",
  "spec": {
    "image": "alpine:latest",
    "command": ["echo"],
    "args": ["hello from harmost"],
    "timeout_seconds": 60
  }
}

### List jobs
GET {{host}}/api/v1/jobs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get one job
GET {{host}}/api/v1/jobs/JOB_ID_HERE
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Get job logs
GET {{host}}/api/v1/jobs/JOB_ID_HERE/logs
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

# ─── Device flow (what `agent pair` does under the hood) ─────────────────────

### 1. Start device flow (unauthenticated — the agent calls this)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/device/authorize

### 2. Approve the device (authenticated — the frontend /device page calls this)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/device/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "user_code": "USER_CODE_FROM_STEP_1"
}

### 3. Poll for the agent token (unauthenticated — the agent polls this)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/device/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "device_code": "DEVICE_CODE_FROM_STEP_1"
}
